Conformance of independent implementations

Run on 2026-08-06 against the 52 vectors in test/, through the
harnesses in conformance/.

Each harness calls that implementation's own code and prints the corpus
field format. Where an implementation lacks a check, the harness does
not supply one, so the vector fails and the divergence appears in the
result rather than in a footnote.

Every row is the decode direction only. cmd/check also rebuilds raw
from expect for the forty-four vectors of the encode class, and no
harness implements that direction, so nothing below says anything about
what these implementations write. Findings 3, 5, 9 and 10 are all
places where an implementation would emit bytes the reference rejects,
and all four were found by reading its code after a decode vector
failed, not by the corpus itself.

